course: dictionary
lesson: 4514
title: Headdress and special head decorations
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A headdress is a covering or decoration worn on the head. Look at the clues around the word. «Feathered headdresses and tipis belonged to some Plains peoples, not to all Native Americans.» Feathered tells you the headdress is decorated with feathers, and the sentence links it with a people and their home, so a headdress is something worn with a special meaning.
explain: Headdresses are often worn for ceremonies, celebrations or as part of traditional dress. Words like ceremonial and traditional are clues. A ceremonial headdress is one worn at a special event, such as a festival, a dance or a religious occasion.
explain: Some headdresses are sacred, which means holy or deeply important to a people or religion. They are not costumes to play with. When you write about headdresses, describe them with care and respect, and say whose they are and what they are used for.
fact: A headdress is a covering or decoration worn on the head.
fact: Headdresses are often worn for ceremonies, celebrations or as part of traditional dress.
fact: Feathered war bonnets were worn by some Plains Indian nations, and they are a well-known kind of headdress.
fact: The crowns and nemes of Egyptian pharaohs were headwear too, and they showed power and status.
fact: Some headdresses are sacred, so treat them with respect and do not treat them as costumes.
exercise: «Feathered headdresses and tipis belonged to some Plains peoples, not to all Native Americans.» What is a headdress in this sentence? | *A covering or decoration worn on the head | A tent made of poles and skins | A type of boot worn for riding | A kind of drum
exercise: «Carnival dancers and brides may wear headdresses.» Which phrase means a headdress worn for a special event? | a rain boot | a folding chair | a school bag | *a ceremonial headdress
exercise: Why should we be careful when we talk about a sacred headdress? | *Some headdresses are holy and deserve respect, not play | Sacred things are always cheap | Headdresses are only for dancing | Costumes are always sacred
test: Which of these is a headdress? | *An Egyptian pharaoh's nemes | A wooden spoon | A pencil case | A pair of running shoes
test: «Brides may wear a headdress on their wedding day.» What does headdress mean here? | *A decoration worn on the head | A long white dress | A pair of gloves | A bag for carrying flowers
exam: What is a headdress, and why might someone wear one for a ceremony? | A headdress is a shoe worn at a party | *A headdress is a covering or decoration worn on the head, often for a ceremony or celebration | A headdress is a plain hat worn for rain | A headdress is a kind of tent used in festivals
